1.bug_scenario:
When highlighting TypeScript code that declares generic type parameters with the “extends” keyword (for example:

  interface Prefixer<Something extends string> { … }
  const cloneWith = <T, A extends keyof T, V>(…): … => { … };

) version 10.3.0 of highlight.js fails to recognize and close the generic angle-bracket section. As a result the rest of the file (the parse signature, arrow functions, consts, type aliases, etc.) is mis-highlighted or rendered in the wrong color. In 10.2.1 the same code is highlighted correctly (the generics are isolated and the remainder of the code resumes normal highlighting).
